  "id": "bf44af27-e944-41e6-8ec1-3f15ba18e7c2",
  "title": "Unified Framework for Medical Image Segmentation with Uncertainty-Aware Techniques",
  "summary": "arXiv Computer Vision reports a post-hoc framework (SegWithU) that augments a frozen segmentation backbone with a lightweight uncertainty head, modeling uncertainty as perturbation energy in a compact probe space. It achieves state-of-the-art performance across multiple benchmark datasets, demonstrating robustness and efficiency in reliability-aware medical segmentation. The other report discusses the differentiable shift-variant FBP model for cone-beam CT, highlighting its efficiency and robustness under challenging acquisition settings.",
